```json
{
  "tool": "read_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "data/patches/D0000/train.csv"
  }
}
```

Now I understand the data structure. Each dataset has 32 features and a label (0-3) representing foreground fraction buckets. Let me create the analysis code to train segmentation baselines on 4 selected datasets.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "mkdir -p code outputs report/images"
  }
}
```

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "if not exist code mkdir code && if not exist outputs mkdir outputs && if not exist report\\images mkdir report\\images"
  }
}
```

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "python code/cell_segmentation_benchmark.py"
  }
}
```

The analysis is complete. Let me verify the outputs and then write the comprehensive research report.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "dir outputs && dir report\\images"
  }
}
```

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "dir report && type report\\report.md | findstr \"^#\" | head -20"
  }
}
```

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "echo \"=== Report Structure ===\" && type report\\report.md | findstr \"^#\" && echo. && echo \"=== All Files ===\" && dir /s /b"
  }
}
```
